WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.733
Agentic QA, autonomous testing agents.

2
00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.113
Nobody scripts the exact clicks.

3
00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:09.167
The agent decides them live, in a real browser.

4
00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:16.333
This is the same agent loop as any tool using agent, with a live browser as the environment.

5
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:20.533
First, it perceives the page, using the DOM and a screenshot.

6
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:25.900
Then it plans the next action toward a stated goal, like sign up and reach the dashboard.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.174
Then it acts by clicking, typing, or navigating.

8
00:00:29.174 --> 00:00:32.767
It repeats until the goal is reached or a step limit hits.

9
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.533
How does it differ from a script?

10
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:38.933
A script follows a click path someone wrote in advance.

11
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.700
An agent works out the path live, so it finds routes nobody anticipated.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.167
That is also why it is slower, costlier, and varies from run to run.

13
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.867
Here is a real example.

14
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.833
The agent is only told to check out as a guest.

15
00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:57.833
Mid checkout, it presses browser back, just out of curiosity.

16
00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.739
The cart is silently emptied with no error.

17
00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:04.800
No script tested pressing back, because nobody thought to write it.

18
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.933
So the right pattern is discovery, not replacement.

19
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:10.600
The agent explores.

20
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.400
When it finds a real bug, turn that exact path into a deterministic script.

21
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.880
It joins the regression suite, and is caught for free from then on, instead of by chance.

22
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.033
That's the loop with test generation.

23
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:27.033
The mistake is letting the agent replace the suite.

24
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:31.167
Let it discover, and let deterministic scripts do the regression work.

25
00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.128
Let's recap.

26
00:01:33.128 --> 00:01:36.300
The agent perceives, plans, and acts in a browser.

27
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.067
It finds paths scripts never anticipated.

28
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.767
But it is slower and non deterministic.

29
00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.078
So turn what it finds into scripted tests.

30
00:01:45.078 --> 00:01:47.300
Next up: AI in the CI pipeline.
